# Roster et al. (2026)  [arXiv:2607.27887]
# The eROSITA X-ray luminosity function of active galactic nuclei.
#
# Binned Vmax estimates from their Fig. 5, one file per redshift panel.
# Estimator: Page & Carrera (2000) Vmax, corrected for the selection
#     function.  Survey: DR2 Vmax.
# Band: rest-frame 2-10 keV. The sample is selected in the observed
#     0.2-2.3 keV band; their Sec. 3.4 converts the luminosities to
#     2-10 keV "to be consistent with most works from literature", and
#     the x-axis of their Fig. 5 is rest-frame log L_2-10keV.
#     The fit is not corrected for intrinsic absorption.
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7.
# Bins: 1 dex wide (44.0-45.0), tabulated at the bin centre.
# Phi convention: log10(dPhi/dlogLX / Mpc^-3 dex^-1).
#
# PROVENANCE: Roster et al. publish these points only as a figure (no
#     table, and no data files in the arXiv source). The values were
#     recovered from the vector coordinates of Fig. 5 in the arXiv
#     source package -- exact marker and error-bar-cap positions, not
#     pixel digitisation. Cross-check: the recovered x error bars land
#     on exactly round 1 dex bin edges and log Phi = -5 falls exactly
#     on their labelled tick.
#
# logLX  log_Phi  +dlog_Phi  -dlog_Phi
44.5 -6.969 0.042 0.046
